EXT. CHERRY ORCHARD IN BLOSSOM - DAY

Pink petals on the wind. A weathered fence. A stone farmhouse with the shutters closed.

Two men sit on the porch.

LAZARUS BARNABY-OKORO (50s, shirtsleeves, suspenders, sharp eyes) whittles. Slow strokes.

HEZEKIAH "HEZ" ARRINGTON-CHEN (60s, white mustache, bad leg stretched out) fans himself with a hat.

A mockingbird sings. Petals fall.

HEZ
Pretty.

LAZARUS
Pretty.

Silence.

HEZ
Used to hate cherries.

LAZARUS
You never said.

HEZ
Didn't have to.

He fans himself. Lazarus sets down the knife.

LAZARUS
Hez.

HEZ
Mm.

LAZARUS
Eleven years.

HEZ
Twelve in August.

LAZARUS
Twelve.

Hez nods. A petal lands on his boot. He brushes it off.

HEZ
You ever think she'd come back?

LAZARUS
No.

HEZ
Me neither.

A quiet. The mockingbird stops. The wind drops. The orchard holds its breath.

HEZ (CONT'D)
Funny how the birds go quiet.

LAZARUS
Mm.

HEZ
Before weather.

LAZARUS
Before something.

Lazarus rises. Walks to the porch rail. Looks down the lane.

Dust, far off. One rider. Coming slow.

LAZARUS (CONT'D)
Company.

Hez struggles up. Takes his hat. Stands beside him. They watch together.

The rider reaches the gate. Stops. A woman. Black dress, black hat, a rifle across the saddle. She dismounts.

Her name is PRUDENCE LOWELL-ADEYEMI (40s, dust-streaked, hard-eyed). She walks to the porch. Stops at the bottom step.

PRUDENCE
Lazarus.

LAZARUS
Prudence.

PRUDENCE
Hezekiah.

HEZ
Ma'am.

She lets the rifle hang.

PRUDENCE
You thought I was dead.

LAZARUS
We hoped.

PRUDENCE
That's honest.

HEZ
Pru, we can talk--

PRUDENCE
We talked. Twelve years ago. On this porch.

She climbs one step.

PRUDENCE (CONT'D)
You said you'd sell the land and split it.

LAZARUS
We did.

PRUDENCE
You said you'd send my share.

LAZARUS
It never--

PRUDENCE
It never came.

Lazarus and Hez exchange a look. Hez's hand drifts toward his hat.

HEZ
Pru, I don't know what you think--

PRUDENCE
I think the orchard is mine.

Petals swirl. Lazarus's hand goes still on the rail.

LAZARUS
It's mine, Pru. I paid.

PRUDENCE
With what?

Silence. She climbs another step.

PRUDENCE (CONT'D)
With my share.

LAZARUS
(low)
Pru.

PRUDENCE
I'm not here to kill you.

HEZ
Thank God.

PRUDENCE
I'm here to sit.

She climbs the last step. Looks at the empty chair. Sits. Lays the rifle across her knees.

PRUDENCE (CONT'D)
Pour me a drink, Hez.

Hez stares at her. Slowly reaches for the jug. Pours. His hand trembles. She takes the cup.

She drinks. Sets it down.

PRUDENCE (CONT'D)
Now. Tell me about the cherries.

Lazarus turns from the rail. Sits. Picks up the knife. Doesn't whittle. Just holds it.

LAZARUS
They bloom early here.

PRUDENCE
I remember.

The mockingbird starts again, slowly. A petal falls on the rifle barrel. None of them moves to brush it off.
